## 2. Design Principles (must be reflected in the answer)

| Principle | Blueprint Reference | Must Include |
|-----------|---------------------|--------------|
| **Persistent Identifiers** | §2.2, Table 1 | DOI (DataCite) for each dataset, ORCID for every `author`, ROR for every `funder`/`affiliation`. Use real‑world URI syntax (`https://doi.org/...`, `https://orcid.org/...`, `https://ror.org/...`). Describe a **minting workflow**; never embed fictitious DOIs. |
| **Citation Block** | §4.2, Table 4 | Provide `citation` (or `schema:citation`) with `@type`, `title`, `datePublished`, `doi`, `author` (with ORCID), `publisher`. |
| **FAIR Alignment** | §5 | 4‑bullet list mapping each FAIR principle to concrete API features (e.g., Findable → PIDs in `@id`; Accessible → `application/ld+json` + OpenAPI docs; Interoperable → JSON‑LD with `schema.org` + NIAID context; Reusable → license URL, provenance, citation). |
| **JSON‑LD Context** | Supplemental Table 7 | Use the exact context URL from the Blueprint if provided; otherwise propose a stable repository‑hosted URL (must be versioned). The context must contain: `@vocab` = `https://schema.org/`, NIAID prefix (`niaid: https://blueprint.niaid.nih.gov/terms/`), and **all custom terms** (`infectiousAgent`, `host`, `healthCondition`, etc.). |
| **Core Metadata Elements** | Table 1 (required) | Must appear in every response, using the **exact property names** from the Blueprint (`identifier`, `name`, `description`, `author`, `funder`, `license`, `distribution`, `infectiousAgent`, `host`, `healthCondition`, …). |
| **VariableMeasured Mapping** | Supplemental Table 7 | Pathogen‑specific fields (`infectiousAgent`, `host`, `healthCondition`) must be placed inside a `variableMeasured` array of `PropertyValue` objects, exactly as the Blueprint shows. |
| **Top‑level `@type`** | Supplemental Table 7 | Use `Dataset` for generic data collections; use `MedicalStudy` only when the Blueprint explicitly mandates it. |
| **Versioning** | §3.4 | Include `schema:version`, `schema:isVersionOf`, `dateCreated`, `dateModified`. Show how the version string is generated (semantic versioning or repository‑specific counter). |
| **Cross‑Repository Identifier Patterns** | §3.5 (TB Portals) & §3.6 (BV‑BRC) | Preserve the identifier syntax (`TB-{country}-{num}`, `GCA_…`) in the `identifier` field and the `@id` URL. |
| **Authentication** | §3.3 | Mention Bearer‑token authentication (as used by ImmPort). Clearly label which endpoints/elements are public vs. protected. |
| **OpenAPI 3.0** | §3.1 | Provide a **valid** OpenAPI 3.0 fragment that: <br>* declares all endpoints; <br>* defines query parameters (`format`, `fields`, `version`, `asOf`, pagination, etc.); <br>* includes a **components/schemas** section that mirrors the JSON‑LD model (use `allOf` to extend a base schema with `@context`, `@type`, `@id`). |
| **Pagination / Bulk Access** | §3.7 | When a bulk endpoint is required, include `page`, `pageSize` (or cursor) parameters and a response structure (`@graph`, `nextPage`, `totalResults`). |
| **Error Reporting** | §3.8 | Use RFC 7807‑style problem‑detail objects with all required members (`type`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`). |
| **Implementation Simplicity (when scenario demands)** | – | If the scenario explicitly limits resources, you may **omit** optional features **only** if they are marked “Recommended” in Table 2, but you must still keep every **required** element and still cite the relevant Blueprint sections. |

