## 6. Example of a Perfect Minimal Output (Skeleton)

> **Do not copy this verbatim; use it only as a structural guide.**  
> Replace placeholders (e.g., `<REPO_NAME>`, `<API_BASE_URL>`) with the actual repository details.

```markdown
## <REPO_NAME> – Minimal Metadata API (Blueprint‑Compliant)

### FAIR Alignment
- **Findable** – Persistent DOIs in `@id`/`identifier`; searchable via `/api/<resource>/{id}` (see Blueprint §5).
- **Accessible** – `application/ld+json` + OpenAPI docs; public metadata, protected binaries behind Bearer token (see Blueprint §3.3).
- **Interoperable** – JSON‑LD using `schema.org` + NIAID context; standard vocabularies (DCAT, DCTerms, NCBI Taxon) (see Blueprint §5).
- **Reusable** – Clear `license` URL, provenance fields (`dateCreated`, `dateModified`), citation block (see Blueprint §4.2).

### PID Strategy
- **Dataset DOI** – Minted via DataCite REST API on publication; pattern `https://doi.org/10.<repo‑prefix>/<type>.<id>.v<version>` (e.g., `https://doi.org/10.1234/immport.sdy998.v2.1`).  
- **Authors** – Collect ORCID at submission; validate via ORCID API (`https://orcid.org/0000‑0002‑1825‑0097`).  
- **Funders** – Map grant numbers to ROR URIs (`https://ror.org/02x2f7339`).  
- **Repository‑specific IDs** – Use native patterns (e.g., ImmPort `SDY998`, TB Portals `TB‑US‑00123`, BV‑BRC `GCA_000001405.1`) (see Blueprint §3.5‑§3.6).

### Recommended Endpoints
| Method | Path | Description | Auth |
|--------|------|-------------|------|
| GET | `/api/<resource>/{id}` | Retrieve single resource metadata (JSON or JSON‑LD) | Bearer (public fields) |
| GET | `/api/<resource>/{id}/versions` | List all versions | Bearer |
| GET | `/api/<resource>/{id}/versions/{ver}` | Retrieve a specific version | Bearer |
| POST | `/api/query` | Bulk search with filters | Bearer |
| GET | `/api/context` | Return the Blueprint JSON‑LD context | Public |
| GET | `/api/openapi.json` | OpenAPI 3.0 document | Public |

### Query Parameters (for `/api/<resource>/{id}`)
| Name | In | Type | Required | Description |
|------|----|------|----------|-------------|
| `format` | query | string | No | `json` (default) or `jsonld` |
| `fields` | query | string | No | Comma‑separated whitelist for sparse responses |
| `version` | query | string | No | Explicit version ID (e.g., `v2.1`) |
| `asOf` | query | string (ISO‑8601) | No | Snapshot at given timestamp |
| `page` | query | integer | No | Page number (default 1) |
| `pageSize` | query | integer | No | Results per page (default 20, max 100) |
| `cursor` | query | string | No | Cursor token for next page (Blueprint §3.7) |

