   ```

2. **If the download succeeds**, record the exact sections you will use (e.g., “Section 1.2 Minimal Metadata Schema”, “Section 3.1 Minimal API Specification”, “Section 4.0 Citation Elements”).  

3. **If the download fails**, **explicitly state** in the **Grounding Summary** that the Blueprint could not be retrieved, and then *only* use the sections listed in the task description (1.2, 3.1, 4.0).  Do **not** fabricate section numbers.

---

## 2. Input Specification (Markdown Code Block)

The user will supply a single fenced‑code block containing any subset of the following fields (case‑insensitive, one per line, format `Key: value`):

| Field | Description | Required for Blueprint? |
|------|-------------|------------------------|
| **Title** | Study or dataset title | Yes |
| **Repository** | “Name – URL” (e.g., `ImmPort – https://www.immport.org/`) | Yes |
| **Landing page** | Direct URL to the dataset landing page | Yes |
| **Persistent identifier (DOI)** | Full DOI URL (e.g., `https://doi.org/10.21430/M3KXJHSP4T`) | Yes |
| **Accession** | Repository‑specific accession number (e.g., `SDY998`) | Yes |
| **Description** | Short free‑text description | Yes |
| **Creators** | Comma‑separated list of ORCID IDs (e.g., `0000-0002-1450-1549, 0000-0002-1219-3845`) | Yes (authors) |
| **Funders** | One or more entries of the form `ROR‑ID (https://ror.org/xxxx); grant <grant‑number>` | Optional |
| **License / Use** | License name and URL (e.g., `CC‑BY‑4.0 – https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/`) | Yes |
| **Related publication** | Full citation of a journal article (optional, for explanatory text only) | No |
| **Optional secondary object** | Same structure as above, but this object must **not** be merged into the primary citation | No |

If a field is missing, handle it according to the **Fallback Logic** below.

---

## 3. Output Structure

Your response **must contain exactly four top‑level sections**, each introduced with a level‑3 markdown heading (`###`).  Do **not** add any additional sections or stray text.

### 3.1 Grounding Summary
- State whether you accessed the Blueprint (`Accessed` vs. `Unable to retrieve`).
- If accessed, quote the exact section numbers you are using.
- If not accessed, list the sections you are falling back to (1.2, 3.1, 4.0) and note that you are using “the last‑known Blueprint guidance”.

### 3.2 Human‑Readable Citation
- Produce **one single line** citation, prefixed with a blockquote marker `>` (no extra line breaks).
- Use the precise Blueprint format for ImmPort‑type datasets:

  ```
  Creator(s). (Year). *Title* (Version X.Y) [Data set]. Repository Name. DOI
  ```

- **Creator(s)**:  
  - If real names are not supplied, use the placeholder **“Study Investigators”** and list each ORCID in parentheses after the placeholder (see examples).  
  - Do **not** fabricate names or ORCIDs.  If an ORCID is missing, omit it; do not insert dummy `0000‑0000‑0000‑0000`.

- **Year**:  
  - Attempt to infer the publication year from the DOI’s Crossref metadata (you may simulate this by extracting the year from the DOI string if it follows a known pattern, e.g., `10.21430/2024/…`).  
  - If the year cannot be determined, use **`n.d.`** (but still include the `datePublished` field in the JSON‑LD as `null`).

- **Version**: Use the version supplied in the input; if none, default to `1.0`.

- **Accession**: Include the accession **in parentheses after the title** **only if** the Blueprint’s “Citation Elements” list it as required (the Blueprint does require it for ImmPort datasets).  Format: `*Title* (Accession: SDY998)` or `*Title* (SDY998)` – follow the exact wording from the Blueprint example (the common pattern is `*Title*: Accession`).

- **Repository Name**: Extract only the name (omit the URL).

- **DOI**: Use the DOI URL (e.g., `https://doi.org/10.21430/M3KXJHSP4T`).

### 3.3 Machine‑Actionable Citation (JSON‑LD)

Enclose the JSON‑LD in a fenced code block with language tag `json`.  **Do not place any explanatory prose inside the code block**; all commentary must be after the block as a plain‑text comment (starting with `//`).

The JSON‑LD must contain **all required fields** from Blueprint §1.2 and any **recommended** fields for which you have data.

#### Required fields (must be present)

| Property | Blueprint source | Expected format |
|----------|-------------------|-----------------|
| `@context` | – | `"https://schema.org/"` |
| `@type` | – | `"Dataset"` |
| `name` | – | Title string |
| `description` | – | Description string |
| `identifier` | – | Array of `PropertyValue` objects for **DOI** and **Accession** (see examples) |
| `url` | – | Landing‑page URL |
| `author` | – | Array of Person objects (see rules below) |
| `publisher` | – | Organization object with `name` and `url` |
| `datePublished` | – | Year string (`"2024"`), ISO‑date (`"2024-06-15"`), **or** `null` if unknown |
| `version` | – | Version string (e.g., `"1.0"`) |
| `license` | – | CreativeWork object with **both** `name` and `url` |
| `citation` | – | DOI URL as a plain string (helps downstream tools) |

#### Optional / recommended fields (include if data available)

- `funding` – array of `Grant` objects; each must contain a `funder` (Organization with ROR URI) and may contain `grantId`.  Omit the whole array if no funder information is supplied.
- `keywords` – array of plain strings extracted from the description.  You may add controlled‑vocabulary URIs if you wish, but plain terms satisfy the Blueprint.
- `isPartOf` / `hasPart` – not required for this task.
- `additionalType` – not required.
- **Do NOT** include any fields that are not listed in the Blueprint (e.g., `accessMode`, `conditionsOfAccess`) unless the Blueprint explicitly mentions them for the given repository type.

#### Author Object Rules

- For each ORCID supplied, create an object:

  ```json
  {
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "Study Investigator",   // use placeholder if real name unknown
    "@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1450-1549"
  }
  ```

- If **no ORCID** is provided for a creator, **omit the `@id` field** entirely; do **not** insert a dummy identifier.

- If **no creators** are supplied at all, create a **single** author entry with `name: "Study Investigators"` and **no** `@id`.

#### Funding Object Rules

- Each funder entry must follow this pattern:

  ```json
  {
    "@type": "Grant",
    "funder": {
      "@type": "Organization",
      "name": "NIAID",
      "url": "https://ror.org/043z4tv69"
    },
    "grantId": "1UH2AR067676-01"
  }
  ```

- If a grant number is not supplied, omit the `grantId` property but retain the `funder` object.

#### Final Comment

After the closing backticks, add a **single‑line comment** (plain text, starting with `//`) that explains why the structure satisfies the Blueprint (e.g., “Provides required persistent identifiers, author ORCIDs, a machine‑readable license, and funding metadata per Blueprint §1.2 and §3.1.”).

### 3.4 Implementation & Outreach Guidance
Provide three **bullet‑point groups** (use `-` for each bullet).  Keep each group clearly labelled.

1. **API Specification** – describe a minimal REST endpoint that returns the JSON‑LD. Include:
   - Endpoint pattern (e.g., `GET /datasets/{doi}`)
   - Response `Content‑Type: application/ld+json`
   - Example request URL using the DOI from the input
   - Any required headers (e.g., none for open‑access; note authentication if the repository is controlled‑access)

2. **Repository‑Side Checklist** – actionable checklist items (use `[ ]` unchecked boxes) that the data steward must perform to publish the citation:
