## REQUIRED OUTPUT STRUCTURE

Your response **must contain exactly four sections**, each headed with a level‑3 markdown heading (`###`). The sections must appear in the order below and must follow the formatting rules that follow each heading.

### 1. Grounding Summary
- State whether you **successfully retrieved** the Blueprint document at  
  `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/go-fair-us/ai-blueprint-core/refs/heads/master/docs/BluePrint/NIAID_Blueprint_v2_26Sep2025_forExternal.md`.
- If you retrieved it, **quote the exact section numbers** you are using (e.g. “Section 1.2 Minimal Metadata Schema”, “Section 3.1 Minimal API Specification”, “Section 4.2 Citation Elements”).  
- If you could **not** retrieve the file, explicitly say so and note that you are using the **last‑known Blueprint guidance** (the sections listed above).

### 2. Human‑Readable Citation
- Produce **one single line** citation string, **prefixed with `>`** (blockquote).  
- Use the exact Blueprint format for ImmPort‑type datasets:

```
Creator(s). (Year). *Title* (Version X.Y) [Data set]. Repository Name. DOI
```

  - **Creator(s)**: list the authors in “Surname Initial.” form if names are known; otherwise use **“Study Investigators”** (repeat once, regardless of how many ORCIDs are supplied).  
  - **Year**: extract the publication year from the DOI metadata if you can; otherwise use `n.d.`.  
  - **Title**: if the Blueprint’s “Citation Elements” list **Accession** as required, prepend the accession to the title separated by a colon and a space (e.g. `SDY998: AMP Rheumatoid Arthritis Phase 1`).  
  - **Version**: include only if a version number is supplied in the input; otherwise omit the entire “(Version X.Y)” parenthetical.  
  - **Repository Name**: the plain name (no URL).  
  - **DOI**: use the **full DOI URL** (e.g. `https://doi.org/10.21430/M3KXJHSP4T`).

- Do **not** add any trailing punctuation after the DOI.

