### 1. Extract Required Blueprint Content  

| Blueprint Section | What to Extract (copy verbatim unless otherwise noted) |
|-------------------|-------------------------------------------------------|
| **Section 1 – Definitions** | Definition of **“Point of Contact for Outreach and Training”** and any rule limiting the number of contacts. |
| **Section 2 – Requirements for the POC** | • List of mandatory responsibilities (bullet‑point text). <br>• Required contact‑channel format (e.g., email alias, ticket system). <br>• Service‑Level Agreement (SLA) – response times, escalation. <br>• Recommended qualifications (e.g., knowledge of FAIR, ORCID, ROR). |
| **Section 3 – Metadata Requirements** | • **All required minimal metadata elements** (e.g., `@type`, `identifier`, `name`, `description`, `creator` (ORCID), `datePublished`, `license`, `accessLevel`, `publisher` (ROR), `keywords`, `measurementTechnique`). <br>• **All recommended elements** (e.g., `funding`, `version`, `dateModified`). |
| **Section 4 – Citation Requirements** | • Exact citation template (including required fields and ordering). <br>• Whether the DOI must be prefixed with `doi:`. |
| **Section 5 – API / Harvesting Guidance** | • Preferred API style (REST, JSON‑LD, OpenAPI). <br>• Required endpoint patterns, pagination, authentication. <br>• Preferred harvesting protocol for the Discovery Portal (e.g., OAI‑PMH, OpenAPI, or a specific JSON‑LD endpoint). |
| **Section 6 – Integration with the Discovery Portal** | • Expectations for persistent identifiers, linking back to the portal, and any additional interoperability constraints. |

*If any of the above sections are missing or ambiguous, note the gap in the final answer and proceed with the best‑fit interpretation, clearly marking it as an assumption.*

