If you cannot retrieve that document, **state that explicitly** before proceeding.

Your task is to **generate a complete, valid JSON‑LD author block** for a digital object (e.g., an ImmPort study, a dataset in a repository, etc.) **conforming to the NIAID Blueprint recommendations**.  

---

### 1. Input you will receive
The input will contain the following sections (order may vary, but headings will be recognizable):

| Section | What it contains |
|---------|------------------|
| **Digital object** | Title of the dataset / study, landing‑page URL, DOI (or other persistent identifier). |
| **Principal investigators / creators** | A bullet list of ORCID IDs (always provided). For each ORCID you may also receive the affiliation name; if an institutional ROR can be resolved, the ROR will be supplied, otherwise you must attempt to resolve it (or leave it out). No person name is provided unless the source table includes it. |
| **Organizational contributors / hosting** | One or more organizations that contributed or host the data. For each you will receive the organization name and, when known, the ROR ID (full URL). |
| **Formatting notes** | Specific guidance on how the Blueprint wants the structure (e.g., prefer `Person`/`Organization` types, include ORCID as a resolvable URL, include ROR, flag the corresponding author, etc.). |

---

### 2. Required output structure (must be exactly followed)

Your output must be a **single JSON‑LD object** that meets the Blueprint **“Minimal Metadata Schema”** and the **“Author Guidance”**. Produce **only the JSON**, no extra prose, no comments.

#### Top‑level object
```json
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org/",
  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "<Digital object title>",
  "description": "<Brief description – you may copy the title if none is given>",
  "url": "<Landing‑page URL>",
  "identifier": {
    "@type": "PropertyValue",
    "propertyID": "DOI",
    "value": "<DOI without the https://doi.org/ prefix>",
    "url": "https://doi.org/<DOI>"
  },
  "datePublished": "<YYYY-MM-DD> (if not supplied, omit)",
  "license": "<License URL or name if supplied, otherwise omit>",
  "author": [ … ],          // see below
  "creator": [ … ]          // identical to “author” per Blueprint Table 1; include both
}
```

*If `datePublished` or `license` are not provided in the input, simply omit those fields.*

#### `author` / `creator` array
Each entry must be either a **`Person`** or an **`Organization`** object.

**Person object (required fields)**
```json
{
  "@type": "Person",
  "name": "<display name if supplied; otherwise a placeholder keyed by ORCID>",
  "identifier": {
    "@type": "PropertyValue",
    "propertyID": "ORCID",
    "value": "<ORCID without dashes>",
    "url": "https://orcid.org/<ORCID>"
  },
  "affiliation": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "<Affiliation name>",
    "identifier": {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "propertyID": "ROR",
      "value": "<ROR ID without the https://ror.org/ prefix>",
      "url": "https://ror.org/<ROR ID>"
    }
  },
  "role": {
    "@type": "Role",
    "roleName": "<One of: Principal Investigator, Co‑Investigator, Corresponding Author, Data Curator, etc.>"
  }
}
```
*If the affiliation ROR is unknown, omit the `identifier` block but keep the `name`.*

**Organization object (required fields)**
```json
{
  "@type": "Organization",
  "name": "<Organization name>",
  "identifier": {
    "@type": "PropertyValue",
    "propertyID": "ROR",
    "value": "<ROR ID without the https://ror.org/ prefix>",
    "url": "https://ror.org/<ROR ID>"
  },
  "role": {
    "@type": "Role",
    "roleName": "<e.g., Hosting Repository, Funding Agency, Consortium, etc.>"
  },
  "url": "<Official website URL if known>"
}
```
*If a ROR for an organization is not supplied, omit the `identifier` block.*

#### Ordering & special flags
* The **Corresponding Author** (if any) **must be first** in the `author`/`creator` arrays and must have `"roleName": "Corresponding Author"`.
* Follow the order given in the input: list all principal investigators first (in the order they appear), then any additional persons, then organizational contributors.

#### Identifier formatting details
* **ORCID** – store the raw 16‑digit identifier without dashes in the `value` field; the `url` must be the fully resolvable form (`https://orcid.org/xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx`).
* **ROR** – store the raw ROR string (e.g., `043z4tv69`) in the `value` field; the `url` must be `https://ror.org/<ROR>`.

#### Placeholder for missing person names
If a person's display name is not provided, create a placeholder name that clearly references the ORCID, e.g.:
```json
"name": "Person (ORCID: 0000000214530149)"
