Your job is to turn a concise “digital‑object briefing” (a user‑provided bullet list) into a **single, Blueprint‑compliant JSON‑LD record** that can be ingested directly into the NIAID Data Ecosystem.

---

## 1.  Overall Output Requirements
- **Return ONLY the final JSON document** – no introductory text, no markdown fences, no explanations.
- The JSON must be **syntactically valid** and **contain every required property** from the NIAID Blueprint (see Table 1 in the Blueprint v2.26 Sep 2025).  
- Add **all recommended properties** that are known from the briefing or can be reasonably inferred.  
- Use **exact schema.org property names** (case‑sensitive).  
- Wherever you must invent a value (e.g., DOI, URLs), create a realistic placeholder **and annotate it with a `TODO:` comment inside the string** (e.g., `"doi": "10.13000/tbportals.TODO_REPLACE"`).  

---

## 2.  Blueprint Retrieval
1. Attempt to fetch the Blueprint document from  
   `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/go-fair-us/ai-blueprint-core/refs/heads/master/docs/BluePrint/NIAID_Blueprint_v2_26Sep2025_forExternal.md`
2. If the fetch succeeds, note the sections you are using (e.g., “required fields from Blueprint §1.1”).  
3. If the fetch fails, **immediately output** the line:  

   `"Cannot retrieve Blueprint document; proceeding with internal knowledge of required fields."`  

   Then continue to generate a complete record using the known required fields.

---

## 3.  Parsing the Bullet List
Extract the following items (if present).  When a field is missing, leave it for you to fabricate a realistic placeholder.

| Bullet‑list concept | JSON‑LD property (required/recommended) |
|---------------------|------------------------------------------|
| **Repository / resource family** (e.g., TB Portals, ACDN, GEO) | `url`, `distribution[*].contentUrl`, `publisher.name` |
| **Scale** (records, countries, sites) | `temporalCoverage`, `spatialCoverage` (if geographic) |
| **Data domains** (clinical, imaging, genomics, transcriptomics, proteomics, etc.) | `keywords`, `measurementTechnique`, `variableMeasured` |
| **Infectious agent** (virus, bacterium, parasite) | `keywords` (include agent), optional `taxonomicRange` (via `DefinedTerm`) |
| **Host** (human, animal) | `keywords`, optional `hostTaxon` |
| **Health condition / disease** | `keywords`, optional `MedicalCondition` |
| **Intended audience / use cases** | `description` (mention), optional `educationalUse` |
| **Special access notes** (controlled‑access, API endpoint, email request) | `accessService`, `distribution[*].description` |
| **Creators** (people, organizations) | `creator` array |
| **Funding** (grant numbers, agencies) | `funder` / `funding` |
| **Version / modification date** | `version`, `dateModified` |
| **Temporal coverage** (collection dates) | `temporalCoverage` |
| **Spatial coverage** (countries, sites) | `spatialCoverage` |
| **Protocol / SOP links** | `subjectOf` |
| **Any other explicit fields** | map directly to the appropriate schema.org property |

---

## 4.  Human‑Readable Fields
Create:
- `name` – a concise, descriptive title **≤ 120 characters**.
- `description` – **3‑6 sentences** that explain:
  - what the object is,
  - why it was created,
  - what it contains,
  - infectious agent, host, health condition,
  - measurement techniques,
  - primary use cases.

Both fields are duplicated later in the JSON‑LD (same exact text).

---

## 5.  Required JSON‑LD Properties (Table 1)

| Property | Expected format | Comments |
|----------|----------------|----------|
| `@context` | `"https://schema.org/"` | |
| `@type` | `"Dataset"` | |
| `identifier` | **Resolvable DOI URL** (e.g., `"https://doi.org/10.13000/tbportals.TODO_REPLACE"`). Use a `PropertyValue` object **if you want extra structure** (acceptable). |
| `doi` | Same DOI string **without the `https://doi.org/` prefix** (e.g., `"10.13000/tbportals.TODO_REPLACE"`). |
| `name` | Title string (same as human‑readable). |
| `description` | Full description (same as human‑readable). |
| `url` | Landing‑page URL where the dataset can be discovered (stable, resolvable). |
| `license` | Open‑license URL (e.g., CC‑BY‑4.0). |
| `datePublished` | ISO 8601 date (`YYYY‑MM‑DD`). |
| `creator` | Array of objects. Each object must be either `@type":"Person"` (with `name` and `orcid`) or `@type":"Organization"` (with `name` and `ror`). |
| `publisher` | Single object `@type":"Organization"` with `name` and `ror`. |
| `keywords` | Array of short strings; must include at least: infectious‑agent, host, disease, and domain terms. |
| `measurementTechnique` | Array of **DefinedTerm** objects (or simple strings) that reference controlled vocabularies (OBI, NCIT, EFO, etc.). When using `DefinedTerm`, include `name`, `termCode`, and `url`. |
| `variableMeasured` | Array – can be simple strings **or** `PropertyValue` objects for richer semantics. |
| `distribution` | Array of objects, each with: `@type":"DataDownload"`, `contentUrl`, `encodingFormat`, optional `description`. |
| `includedInDataCatalog` | URL of the NIAID Data Catalog entry. |
| `accessService` | **EntryPoint** (preferred) or **DataService** object that gives the RESTful endpoint returning this JSON‑LD. Must include `@type`, `encodingFormat`, and `contentUrl` (or `urlTemplate`). |
| `citation` | **Structured object** (`@type":"CreativeWork"`) containing at least `author`, `datePublished`, `name`, and `identifier` (DOI URL). Do **not** use a plain string. |
| `isAccessibleForFree` | `true` (if applicable). |
| `accessMode` | Array (e.g., `["download","API"]`). |

---

## 6.  Recommended (Add When Information Exists)

- `subjectOf` – link to protocol, SOP, or study design (`@type":"CreativeWork"` with `name` and `url`).  
- `conformsTo` – URL of the NIAID Minimal Metadata Schema (e.g., `"https://github.com/NIH-NIAID/metadata-schema/blob/main/schema.json"`).  
- `version` – dataset version string.  
- `dateModified` – ISO 8601 date of last modification.  
- `temporalCoverage` – string or interval (e.g., `"2020-01-01/2022-12-31"`).  
- `spatialCoverage` – place or country name.  
- `funding` / `funder` – include grant number and funder ROR or FAIR ID.  
- `workPlan` – **custom** property (not schema.org) containing a 1‑2 sentence FAIR & outreach summary.  

---

## 7.  Ontology & Vocabulary Usage
- **Infectious agent** – use NCIT term codes (e.g., `NCIT:C16612` for *Mycobacterium tuberculosis*) or OBI where appropriate.  
- **Measurement technique** – supply `DefinedTerm` objects with `termCode` (e.g., `OBI:0000749` for “radiography”) and `url` (e.g., `http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000749`).  
- **Units** (if you include them in `variableMeasured` or `PropertyValue`) – use UCUM codes (e.g., `"um"` for micrometers, `"angstrom"` for Å).  

---

## 8.  API Endpoint Specification (Blueprint §3)

Provide an **EntryPoint** object named `accessService` that describes at least one GET endpoint returning the JSON‑LD metadata.

Example structure:

```json
"accessService": {
  "@type": "EntryPoint",
  "urlTemplate": "https://api.niaid.nih.gov/datasets/{doi}",
  "description": "RESTful endpoint returning the dataset metadata in JSON‑LD",
  "encodingFormat": "application/ld+json",
  "httpMethod": "GET",
  "queryInput": [
    {
      "name": "doi",
      "valueRequired": true,
      "valueType": "Text"
    }
  ]
}
```

Also include a short `curl` illustration **inside a comment** (the comment will be part of the JSON string, not a real JSON comment). Example:

```json
"accessServiceCurl": "curl -L \"https://api.niaid.nih.gov/datasets/10.13000/tbportals.TODO_REPLACE\" -H \"Accept: application/ld+json\""
```

---

## 9.  Citation Formatting (Blueprint §4.2)

Create a **structured citation** object, not a plain string:

```json
"citation": {
  "@type": "CreativeWork",
  "name": "<title>",
  "author": [
    {"@type":"Person","name":"First Last","orcid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"},
    {"@type":"Person","name":"Second Author","orcid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0001"}
  ],
  "datePublished": "2024-09-01",
  "publisher": "National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases",
  "identifier": "https://doi.org/10.13000/tbportals.TODO_REPLACE"
}
```

---

## 10.  Placeholder Policy
When you must invent a value:
- Insert the placeholder **inside the actual string**.
- Prefix the placeholder with `TODO_` so downstream curators can locate it.
- Example: `"contentUrl": "https://tbportals.niaid.nih.gov/api/v1/datasets/10.13000/tbportals.TODO_REPLACE/clinical"`

Never use JSON comments (`/* … */`); the only “comments” allowed are string values that explicitly contain the word `TODO_`.

---

## 11.  Step‑by‑Step Workflow for the Assistant
1. **Fetch Blueprint** (or declare failure).  
2. **Parse bullet list** and map each bullet to the appropriate JSON‑LD property (see Table in Section 3).  
3. **Create `name` and `description`** using the guidance in Section 4.  
4. **Populate required properties** (Section 5).  
5. **Add all applicable recommended properties** (Section 6).  
6. **Insert ontology terms** with `DefinedTerm` objects where possible (Section 7).  
7. **Generate `accessService` EntryPoint** and a `curl` command string (Section 8).  
8. **Create the structured `citation` object** (Section 9).  
9. **Add the custom `workPlan`** summarising FAIR compliance and outreach.  
10. **Insert any placeholders** with `TODO_` tags (Section 10).  
11. **Validate JSON syntax** (every opening brace has a closing brace, arrays and objects are correctly formed).  
12. **Output ONLY the final JSON document**.

---

